        "title": "chore: align Android icons with favicon mark",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a problem where the Android launcher icon assets still used the older lobster silhouette while the OpenClaw iOS/web mascot uses the newer rounded favicon mark from `ui/public/favicon.svg`.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nRegenerated all Android launcher PNG density assets from the canonical favicon SVG and switched the adaptive icon background to white so the red favicon mascot remains visible. The adaptive foreground keeps the mascot inside Android's safe zone so launcher masks do not crop the mark.\n\n## User Impact\n\nAndroid users see the same OpenClaw favicon mascot as the app identity on launcher surfaces instead of the older white lobster silhouette.\n\nAI-assisted: yes, generated with Codex.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Current reviewed head: `b31c85909f59b305f9d55b7215fbb13dcbf03fb3`.\n- Regenerated `mdpi` through `xxxhdpi` launcher assets from `ui/public/favicon.svg`.\n- Tightened every adaptive foreground density to Android's protected 66/108 mask-safe region; xxxhdpi alpha content is 260 px wide inside the 264 px protected width.\n- Verified PNG dimensions, RGBA encoding, transparent padding, and alpha bounds.\n- Passed `./gradlew :app:testPlayDebugUnitTest :app:testThirdPartyDebugUnitTest :app:assemblePlayDebug`.\n- Installed the Play debug APK on the `openclaw-validation-api36` AVD and visually verified the complete mascot under the launcher's round mask.\n- Passed `git diff --check`.\n- Passed the repository `autoreview` helper against `origin/main` with no actionable findings.\n",
